expression: h.help()
---
Context engineering for coding agents

Usage: instrukt <COMMAND>

Commands:
  agents     Configured profiles and expiring profile/model availability
  config     Read, edit, initialize and validate `instrukt.yaml`
  docs       Validate, list and read documentation snippets
  hooks      Install, remove, inspect and run instrukt's git hook sections
  specs      Use-case coverage, reservation and trace
  blueprint  Structural graph queries (blueprint module)
  todo       The work record and workflow (todos module)
  eval       Evaluation reports from the work record
  events     Discover producer-declared event types and their schemas
  ticks      Scheduled tick status
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Role: focused-handler · class: focused. Scope comes from assignment
instrukt:standing:reactions%2Fprocedure%2Frespond@project%3Afork. Object claims, phase and writer
constraints apply.
Usual capabilities: role: focused-handler; class: focused; grants: docs-read:any, todo-read:any,
artifact-read:any, agents-read:any, config-read:any, repository-read:any, code-check:any,
eval-read:any, events-read:any, installation-read:any
